<title>USA: Mallinckrodt to sell Sensor Systems unit.</title>
<headline>Mallinckrodt to sell Sensor Systems unit.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS, Mo. 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mallinckrodt Group Inc said Monday it signed a definitive agreement for Instrumentation Laboratory to acquire Mallinckrodt Sensor Systems.</p>
<p>The transaction is subject to regulatory approval. Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Mallinckrodt Sensor Systems develops, makes and distributes point-of-care blood gas and electrolyte in vitro diagnostic products.  &quot;Mallinckrodt Sensor Systems is a good business but one that no longer fits with our strategic direction,&quot; C. Ray Holman, chairman, said in a statement.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
